
>> servings: 2

Marinade @sirloin steak{500%g} in @olive oil{}, @salt{} and @pepper{} in a shallow dish. Leave in fridge to marinade.

Preheat oven to 200 degrees Celsius.

Boil @baby potato{700%g} until soft enough to be pierced with a fork.

Coat oven tray in a thin layer of @olive oil{}.

Drain water from potatoes and pour onto oven tray.

With an appropriate implement (???) smash the potatoes so that they are flat but still intact.

Coat top with another small layer of olive oil.

Season with @salt{}.

Cook in oven until crispy and golden. For extra crisp, turn oven onto grill setting at the end for a few minutes.

Time to prepare the greek salad.

Thinly slice @red onion{1} and soak in @lemon juice{}. Put aside for a few minutes.

Roughly dice @cucumber{1/2}, @tomato{4} and place in a bowl.

Cube @feta cheese{150%g} and put aside.

Drain @kalamata olives{200%g}, and de-pip if necessary. Add to bowl with @cucumber{} and @tomato{}.

For the dressing whisk together @olive oil{}, @lemon juice{}, @red wine vinegar{}, @dried oregano{}, @salt{} and @pepper{}. Add ingredients to taste.

Prior to serving, drain @red onion{} and add it to the bowl, add @feta cheese{} to bowl, and dress salad with salad dressing.

Heat a dry pan to medium high heat.

Take marinaded @sirloin steak{} and drain marinade into hot pan. Wait for it to heat up.

Add @sirloin steak{} to pan.

Add @rosemary{2%sprig} to the pan.

Flip @sirloin steak{} every few minutes.

Also, tilt pan, and spoon hot oil onto the top of the steak.

Cook until outside is crispy.

Bench rest for 10 minutes.

Take smashed potatoes out of oven and serve with steak and Greek salad.
